<title>INDIA: TABLE-India's ICICI Q 1 1997/98 net up.</title>
<headline>TABLE-India's ICICI Q 1 1997/98 net up.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	   2,230.0 vs    1,000.0</p>
<p>    Total income	12,440.0 vs    8,970.0</p>
<p>    Fund-based income 11,600.0 vs    8,700.0</p>
<p>    Net capital gains    470.0 vs	 50.0</p>
<p>    Non-fund income	370.0 vs	220.0</p>
<p>    Financial expenses 9,060.0 vs    7,020.0</p>
<p>    Other expenses	 390.0 vs	290.0</p>
<p>    Write offs/provision 550.0 vs	250.0</p>
<p>    Total expenses    10,000.0 vs    7,560.0</p>
<p>    Profit before tax  2,440.0 vs    1,410.0</p>
<p>    Tax			210.0 vs	410.0</p>
<p>Note: The Industrial Credit and Investment Corp of India Ltd (ICICI) is a term-lending bank. It said non-performing assets were 7.80 percent of total assets as on June 30, 1997 against 6.80 percent on March 31, 1997. ICICI recorded a 107 percent growth in loan approvals and 32 percent growth in disbursals in the first quarter over the year ago figures. The results are audited.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
